{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/39755-the-wraith-splats-that-never-were","id":39755,"title":"The Wraith Splats that never were","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-30T20:36:09-08:00","id":39755,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The Wraith Splats that never were","content":"I was reading some of the older threads on everyone's wishes and hopes for Wraith20 and had a look over my own Wraith book list. Wraith and Mage seem to have the fewest city specific books compared to Vampire's By Night series and Werewolf's Rage Across series. Even Changeling has about 4 books focused on very specific regions in geography. Wraith has Necropolis: Atlanta yes, but as we see here in the states every Halloween, all kinds of programs are vying for the title of the Most Haunted Place in the US/Europe/World etc.<br /> <br /> So what would be some really awesome site specific locations you'd like to see/make a Wraith supplement out of?<br /> <br /> Me, I live in San Francisco, and there are a lot of supposedly haunted places around here. But of course the one place that is likely to be the most obviously haunted place of all is Alcatraz Island in the bay. I'd love to see an entire supplement dedicated to the famous Rock and what still goes on there behind the Shroud. I'd even help research and write for it.<br /> <br /> So what places do you think should have their own Wraith book? Have you already run a game revolving around a haunted historical place that could/should be its own Necropolis book??<br /> <br /> Share it wish us!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T21:33:54-08:00","id":39769,"title":"","content":"Haven't yet. But know two locals I'd like to use at one point. Pythian Castle and Wilson's Creek Battlefield.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T21:36:20-08:00","id":39776,"title":"","content":"London, Paris (catacombs!), Savannah and New Orleans would all be good spots for Necropoli.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T21:53:58-08:00","id":39783,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">When we played, my troupe lived in the Phoenix Metropolitan Area (PMA, for the purposes of this thread) of Arizona. We used what we knew, so when we weren\u2019t gallivanting through the Tempest, we were in the Shadowlands (and Deadlands, for those who read my troupe\u2019s house rules) of this area.<br /> <br /> I suppose the first thing everyone thinks of when they hear \u201cHaunted Arizona\u201d is Tombstone or Jerome. The PMA consists of several interconnecting satellite cities. Over the years, these cities all melded into one another to form an intriguing blend of suburban sprawls and cosmopolitan hubs, with desolate wastelands on the outskirts. We used several different areas for backdrops, depending on the type of story. That was one of the fun things about Wraith; when you\u2019re dead, anywhere can become interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T23:19:19-08:00","id":39823,"title":"","content":"Don't forget about Ghost Towns, the book that was both for Wild West Werewolf and Wraith! It had five or six ghost towns that were pretty well fleshed-out.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see London and Paris. Both are very old cities, likely large enough and full enough of the dead to support politics as thick as Stygia itself. They also played a pretty big role in The Great War, which I'd love to see elaborated on. (Side note on The Great War; Florence was described as fully sacked and conquered by Spectres, but little more beyond that was said. The Smiling Lord's armies marched on Florence and were nearly wiped out; is the city still in the clutches of Oblivion today?)<br /> <br /> I think New Orleans got a Vampire book, but it would certainly fit Wraith. I can't think of an American city so well made for a game about the dead. You even get the added bonus of some tasty Voodoo mucking across the Shroud and some ghosts with unique Arcanoi. Those old family crypts would make great Haunts, probably hotly contested.<br /> <br /> Moscow would be worth looking at. I imagine the Hierarchy there is especially regimented and harsh, not only as a result of Soviet wraith but also due to most likely being the last Necropolis before you hit the Dark Kingdom of Jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T07:22:41-08:00","id":39960,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see Wraith books for New Orleans, Prague, Magadan and Whitby.<br /> I think all four places would have a heavy Restless presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T10:54:26-08:00","id":40062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/39755-the-wraith-splats-that-never-were#post39755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me, I live in San Francisco, and there are a lot of supposedly haunted places around here. But of course the one place that is likely to be the most obviously haunted place of all is Alcatraz Island in the bay. I'd love to see an entire supplement dedicated to the famous Rock and what still goes on there behind the Shroud. I'd even help research and write for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alcatraz did get covered as a haunted place for Wraiths in San Francisco By Night. I'm surprised you didn't bring up the city of Colma, which is mostly graveyards.<br /> As someone in Socal (Ventura): San Francisco already has TWO books (KotE and Changeling), while Los Angeles only has one (Vampire). I personally would love a mega book that would cover the entire state, as there's lots of things for all the supernatural splats there. Or at least cover a different city in California: Like San Diego if you're going for Wraith.<br /> <br /> If you haven't already, pick up the book Weird California by Greg Bishop, Joe Oesterle, and Mike Marinacci. There's tons of stuff in there to use for plothooks, stories, etc.<br /> <br /> I would like something on the East Coast (Say like Connecticut, Maryland, etc.) or a city from Europe.<br /> <br /> In addition to Ghost Towns, there was also the Jade Kingdom Books, which detailed out several places too, as well as Haunts.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> I forgot that Demon also had a book on Los Angeles too. Still, my thought still stands: Do another city in CA than those two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 12-31-2013, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T03:11:37-08:00","id":40436,"title":"","content":"I think a detailed examination of the Wraiths of the great Westward Expansion could have a lot of potential, as most products so far have focused pretty heavily on population centers. Pioneers spreading across the continent leaving behind shallow graves, every new settlement claiming lives before taking root. Displaced indigenous populations permitted to leave no graves at all, fetters stretched across the continent to the ancestral lands they'll never see again. It would be a somber product, even for a Wraith book, but I think it would be fascinating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T12:56:17-08:00","id":41895,"title":"","content":"One word: York.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T13:52:01-08:00","id":41942,"title":"","content":"Wraith had the primary focus of WoD: Tokyo. In said book, there is mention of Mt. Fuji, but nothing having to do with Aokigahara. Just a Dreaming manifestation of the mountain that talks really slowly. And for some reason, an uji of the Demon People is the group talking to it. The mind, it boggles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T18:51:50-08:00","id":42094,"title":"","content":"I would've liked to have seen the Heretics get their own book (I know there's a fan-made one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T17:13:32-08:00","id":42569,"title":"","content":"A Heretics/Far Shores book would be killer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T18:38:24-07:00","id":90541,"title":"","content":"As you live in San Francisco, and as someone who lives in the Bay Area as well, I'm sure you know Winchester Mystery House. I know it's basically a glorified tourist trap, but it's only because it was owned by such an eccentric woman and I've longed wished they would add it into the books. Frankly, Necropolis: Colma just seems necessary <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T08:51:46-07:00","id":90927,"title":"","content":"I think a Book on Swar could easily open up the Setting as much as Dark Kingdom of Jade.<br /> <br /> A Far Shores Book would be at around the top of my lists! So much potential for setting, and exotic mysteries and Arcanoi! It would be great if they expanded on the Demonics/Angelics/Djinn!<br /> <br /> I would Loooove a Necropoli Setting for Singapore, and a Book on Haunted Wilderness in general!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T08:13:58-07:00","id":91640,"title":"","content":"Necropolis Seattle. There is a huge culture around hauntings here and a well-sponsored regular <a href=\"http://seattleghost.com\" target=\"_blank\">ghost tour</a>. <br /> <br /> As for deeper underworld books, I'd love to see a Far Shores book as well. I'd also like to see a book, or at least a large section, specifically on using the Labyrinth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T14:39:45-07:00","id":91855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like to see a book, or at least a large section, specifically on using the Labyrinth.</div> </div> </div> </div> You mean like Doomslayers: Into the Labyrinth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}